  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IN PARTNERSHIP WITH THE ZOOLOGICAL SOCIETY OF SAN DIEGO. THE PURPOSE OF THIS 1-YEAR PROJECT IS TO STRENGTHEN ACTIVE MANAGEMENT OF THE PROPOSED EBO NATIONAL PARK&apos;S CORE GORILLA HABITAT BY CLUBS DES A</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funds under this award are to be used to strengthen active management of the proposed Ebo National Parks core gorilla habitat by Clubs des Amis des Gorilles (CAG), traditional chiefs, and other stakeholders. Activities include: 1) regular community recce transect patrols within the gorilla habitat; 2) recording threats to gorillas and chimpanzees; 3) continuing the process of establishing a no-go zone in the core gorilla habitat; 4) engaging communities through multi-faceted outreach activities; 5) supporting small-scale livelihood-based projects in the three communities; and 6) conducting annual forest-wide recce transect surveys to monitor threats, chimpanzees and other endangered species.</narrative>
  </description>
